    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "THE TEXT",
      "narration_text": "And the text? In published systems, a text encoder turns your prompt into numbers that tilt every prediction. Meta's MusicGen does this: four codebooks, fifty frames a second, and a text encoder called T5 steering the model. In my toy, the words only pick which music it learned from. Calm piano, then busy drums. Neither is copied: the longest stretch it repeats from its training music is a quarter of a second.",
